Terminal Rain (terminal-rain-lightning)

Written by rmaake1 (Ryan), 2025 to 2026:
https://github.com/rmaake1/terminal-rain-lightning

With contributions from:
- plasma (xXBlackPlasmaXx): the slow-motion speed (pull request #7)
- Nihal Kumar (nihalxkumar): the Arch AUR package and its install notes
  (pull request #5)
- the rain and thunder sounds: contributed in pull request #1, described
  there as Pixabay sound effects (Pixabay Content License); rmaake1 cut the
  rain loop and made the thunder variants from them
  (terminal_rain_lightning_assets/sounds/ASSETS.md)

The program, its look, its keys, its options and its sounds are theirs.
Asciiverse ported terminal_rain_lightning.py to Rust (src/main.rs) so it
runs as one binary on Linux, macOS and Windows without Python; the port
follows the script line by line and is released under the same MIT License
(LICENSE). The changes are listed in PATCHES.md.
